---
title: Provider Skills
id: provider-skills
order: 3
description: "Attach hosted, provider-managed skills to code execution and shell tools in TanStack AI so the model can produce documents, run specialised environments, and more."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - provider skills
  - anthropic skills
  - openai skills
  - code execution skills
  - shell tool skills
  - hosted skills
  - container skills
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Skills are hosted, provider-managed capability bundles that the model\nloads on demand and runs inside the provider's server-side sandbox. You\nreference them by a skill ID; the provider handles installation and execution."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not to be confused with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets"}]},{"type":"text","value":", whose snippets\nare TypeScript functions your application generates and runs in its own Code Mode sandbox (a local JS isolate). Provider\nSkills run entirely on the provider's infrastructure."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skills are "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"inert without an execution tool"}]},{"type":"text","value":". The execution tool activates the\nsandbox; skills are additional bundles that run inside it:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic"}]},{"type":"text","value":": skills attach to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeExecutionTool"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]},{"type":"text","value":": skills nest inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shellTool"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openai/tools"},{"type":"text","value":") and\nrequire the Responses API."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You already have a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call working. By the end of this page you will have\nattached a hosted skill to the right execution tool, with the provider handling\nthe rest."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"portable-vs-hosted-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Portable vs hosted skills"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are two ways to give a model skills in TanStack AI, and they solve\ndifferent problems:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Portable skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"link","href":"../skills/agent-skills","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills"}]},{"type":"text","value":") render a catalog\nand let the model call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load_skill"},{"type":"text","value":". They run on any tool-calling model, need\nno server sandbox, and read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SKILL.md"},{"type":"text","value":" from a folder, a bundle, or your own\nstore. Reach for these first."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hosted (provider) skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":", this page, run inside the provider's server-side\nsandbox and are referenced by ID. They are non-portable and require an\nexecution tool, but the provider does the running."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use hosted skills when you need the provider's sandbox (running code, producing\nfiles). Use portable skills for everything else."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The two do not mix in one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call. If you attach hosted skills to a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code_execution"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shell"},{"type":"text","value":" tool and also add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSkills"},{"type":"text","value":", the middleware\nthrows: the model would see two catalogs and two protocols. Pick one delivery\nmode per call."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"anthropic-skills-via-codeexecutiontool","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic: skills via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeExecutionTool"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-install-the-package","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Install the package"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-anthropic\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-anthropic\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-anthropic\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-anthropic\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-anthropic\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-anthropic\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-anthropic\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-anthropic\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-add-the-codeexecutiontool-with-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Add the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeExecutionTool"},{"type":"text","value":" with skills"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeExecutionTool"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools"},{"type":"text","value":", not from the\nadapter root. Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills"},{"type":"text","value":" array as the second argument."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { codeExecutionTool } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    tools: [\n      codeExecutionTool(\n        { type: 'code_execution_20250825', name: 'code_execution' },\n        {\n          skills: [{ type: 'anthropic', skill_id: 'pptx', version: 'latest' }],\n        },\n      ),\n    ],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter automatically:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifts your skills into the request's top-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"container.skills"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter\n(the shape Anthropic's API requires)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attaches the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code-execution-2025-08-25"},{"type":"text","value":" beta header, plus the\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills-2025-10-02"},{"type":"text","value":" beta header when skills are present."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You do not set beta headers manually."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"skill-shape","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skill shape"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each entry in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills"},{"type":"text","value":" array is an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnthropicContainerSkill"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Notes"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'anthropic' | 'custom'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'anthropic'"},{"type":"text","value":" for Anthropic-hosted skills; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'custom'"},{"type":"text","value":" for your own bundles."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skill_id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1–64 characters."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"version"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Specific version string, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'latest'"},{"type":"text","value":" (default when omitted)."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Up to 8 skills per request. The factory throws at call time if you exceed this\nor supply an invalid "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skill_id"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"deprecation-notice","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecation notice"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setting skills via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.container.skills"},{"type":"text","value":" is deprecated. Use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeExecutionTool(config, { skills })"},{"type":"text","value":" instead — the legacy path bypasses the\nautomatic beta-header wiring."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"openai-skills-via-shelltool-responses-api-only","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI: skills via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shellTool"},{"type":"text","value":" (Responses API only)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The OpenAI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shellTool"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"environment"},{"type":"text","value":" object that can carry a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills"},{"type":"text","value":" array. This is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responses API only"}]},{"type":"text","value":"; the Chat Completions API does\nnot support the shell tool."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-install-the-package-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Install the package"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-add-the-shelltool-with-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Add the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shellTool"},{"type":"text","value":" with skills"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { shellTool } from '@tanstack/ai-openai/tools'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n    messages,\n    tools: [\n      shellTool({\n        environment: {\n          type: 'container_auto',\n          skills: [\n            { type: 'skill_reference', skill_id: 'skill_abc', version: '2' },\n          ],\n        },\n      }),\n    ],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"skill-shape-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skill shape"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each entry in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills"},{"type":"text","value":" array is a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SkillReference"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Notes"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'skill_reference'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Always "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'skill_reference'"},{"type":"text","value":" for OpenAI."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skill_id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The skill identifier provided by OpenAI."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"version"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"no"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A positive integer as a string (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'2'"},{"type":"text","value":") or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'latest'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"version"},{"type":"text","value":" is a string, not a number."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"scope","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scope"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Only "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hosted, managed-by-id"}]},{"type":"text","value":" skills are wired by these factories:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type: 'anthropic'"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type: 'custom'"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"type: 'skill_reference'"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inline bundles, local-path references, and upload-API skill creation are not\nhandled by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeExecutionTool"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shellTool"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related-pages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related pages"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../skills/agent-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Portable Agent Skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — the provider-agnostic\nalternative: a catalog plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"load_skill"},{"type":"text","value":", on any tool-calling model."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./provider-tools.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — all native provider tools and the\ntype-level guard that prevents pairing a tool with an unsupported model."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/anthropic.md#codeexecutiontool","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic adapter → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"codeExecutionTool"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/openai.md#shelltool","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI adapter → "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"shellTool"}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"portable-vs-hosted-skills","text":"Portable vs hosted skills","level":2},{"id":"anthropic-skills-via-codeexecutiontool","text":"Anthropic: skills via codeExecutionTool","level":2},{"id":"1-install-the-package","text":"1. Install the package","level":3},{"id":"2-add-the-codeexecutiontool-with-skills","text":"2. Add the codeExecutionTool with skills","level":3},{"id":"skill-shape","text":"Skill shape","level":3},{"id":"deprecation-notice","text":"Deprecation notice","level":3},{"id":"openai-skills-via-shelltool-responses-api-only","text":"OpenAI: skills via shellTool (Responses API only)","level":2},{"id":"1-install-the-package-2","text":"1. Install the package","level":3},{"id":"2-add-the-shelltool-with-skills","text":"2. Add the shellTool with skills","level":3},{"id":"skill-shape-2","text":"Skill shape","level":3},{"id":"scope","text":"Scope","level":2},{"id":"related-pages","text":"Related pages","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nProvider Skills are hosted, provider-managed capability bundles that the model\nloads on demand and runs inside the provider's server-side sandbox. You\nreference them by a skill ID; the provider handles installation and execution.\n\n> **Not to be confused with `@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets`**, whose snippets\n> are TypeScript functions your application generates and runs in its own Code Mode sandbox (a local JS isolate). Provider\n> Skills run entirely on the provider's infrastructure.\n\nSkills are **inert without an execution tool**. The execution tool activates the\nsandbox; skills are additional bundles that run inside it:\n\n- **Anthropic**: skills attach to `codeExecutionTool` (`@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools`).\n- **OpenAI**: skills nest inside `shellTool` (`@tanstack/ai-openai/tools`) and\n  require the Responses API.\n\nYou already have a `chat()` call working. By the end of this page you will have\nattached a hosted skill to the right execution tool, with the provider handling\nthe rest.\n\n---\n\n## Portable vs hosted skills\n\nThere are two ways to give a model skills in TanStack AI, and they solve\ndifferent problems:\n\n- **Portable skills** ([`withSkills`](../skills/agent-skills)) render a catalog\n  and let the model call `load_skill`. They run on any tool-calling model, need\n  no server sandbox, and read `SKILL.md` from a folder, a bundle, or your own\n  store. Reach for these first.\n- **Hosted (provider) skills**, this page, run inside the provider's server-side\n  sandbox and are referenced by ID. They are non-portable and require an\n  execution tool, but the provider does the running.\n\nUse hosted skills when you need the provider's sandbox (running code, producing\nfiles). Use portable skills for everything else.\n\nThe two do not mix in one `chat()` call. If you attach hosted skills to a\n`code_execution` or `shell` tool and also add `withSkills`, the middleware\nthrows: the model would see two catalogs and two protocols. Pick one delivery\nmode per call.\n\n---\n\n## Anthropic: skills via `codeExecutionTool`\n\n### 1. Install the package\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\nvue: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\npreact: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\nangular: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\noctane: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n### 2. Add the `codeExecutionTool` with skills\n\nImport `codeExecutionTool` from `@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools`, not from the\nadapter root. Pass a `skills` array as the second argument.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { codeExecutionTool } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    tools: [\n      codeExecutionTool(\n        { type: 'code_execution_20250825', name: 'code_execution' },\n        {\n          skills: [{ type: 'anthropic', skill_id: 'pptx', version: 'latest' }],\n        },\n      ),\n    ],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nThe adapter automatically:\n\n- Lifts your skills into the request's top-level `container.skills` parameter\n  (the shape Anthropic's API requires).\n- Attaches the `code-execution-2025-08-25` beta header, plus the\n  `skills-2025-10-02` beta header when skills are present.\n\nYou do not set beta headers manually.\n\n### Skill shape\n\nEach entry in the `skills` array is an `AnthropicContainerSkill`:\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `type` | `'anthropic' \\| 'custom'` | yes | `'anthropic'` for Anthropic-hosted skills; `'custom'` for your own bundles. |\n| `skill_id` | `string` | yes | 1–64 characters. |\n| `version` | `string` | no | Specific version string, or `'latest'` (default when omitted). |\n\nUp to 8 skills per request. The factory throws at call time if you exceed this\nor supply an invalid `skill_id`.\n\n### Deprecation notice\n\nSetting skills via `modelOptions.container.skills` is deprecated. Use\n`codeExecutionTool(config, { skills })` instead — the legacy path bypasses the\nautomatic beta-header wiring.\n\n---\n\n## OpenAI: skills via `shellTool` (Responses API only)\n\nThe OpenAI `shellTool` accepts an `environment` object that can carry a\n`skills` array. This is **Responses API only**; the Chat Completions API does\nnot support the shell tool.\n\n### 1. Install the package\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-openai\nvue: @tanstack/ai-openai\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-openai\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-openai\npreact: @tanstack/ai-openai\nangular: @tanstack/ai-openai\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-openai\noctane: @tanstack/ai-openai\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n### 2. Add the `shellTool` with skills\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { shellTool } from '@tanstack/ai-openai/tools'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n    messages,\n    tools: [\n      shellTool({\n        environment: {\n          type: 'container_auto',\n          skills: [\n            { type: 'skill_reference', skill_id: 'skill_abc', version: '2' },\n          ],\n        },\n      }),\n    ],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\n### Skill shape\n\nEach entry in the `skills` array is a `SkillReference`:\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `type` | `'skill_reference'` | yes | Always `'skill_reference'` for OpenAI. |\n| `skill_id` | `string` | yes | The skill identifier provided by OpenAI. |\n| `version` | `string` | no | A positive integer as a string (e.g. `'2'`) or `'latest'`. |\n\nNote: `version` is a string, not a number.\n\n---\n\n## Scope\n\nOnly **hosted, managed-by-id** skills are wired by these factories:\n\n- Anthropic: `type: 'anthropic'` or `type: 'custom'`\n- OpenAI: `type: 'skill_reference'`\n\nInline bundles, local-path references, and upload-API skill creation are not\nhandled by `codeExecutionTool` or `shellTool`.\n\n---\n\n## Related pages\n\n- [Portable Agent Skills](../skills/agent-skills) — the provider-agnostic\n  alternative: a catalog plus `load_skill`, on any tool-calling model.\n- [Provider Tools](./provider-tools.md) — all native provider tools and the\n  type-level guard that prevents pairing a tool with an unsupported model.\n- [Anthropic adapter → `codeExecutionTool`](../adapters/anthropic.md#codeexecutiontool)\n- [OpenAI adapter → `shellTool`](../adapters/openai.md#shelltool)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Provider Skills\nid: provider-skills\norder: 3\ndescription: \"Attach hosted, provider-managed skills to code execution and shell tools in TanStack AI so the model can produce documents, run specialised environments, and more.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - provider skills\n  - anthropic skills\n  - openai skills\n  - code execution skills\n  - shell tool skills\n  - hosted skills\n  - container skills\n---\n\nProvider Skills are hosted, provider-managed capability bundles that the model\nloads on demand and runs inside the provider's server-side sandbox. You\nreference them by a skill ID; the provider handles installation and execution.\n\n> **Not to be confused with `@tanstack/ai-code-mode-snippets`**, whose snippets\n> are TypeScript functions your application generates and runs in its own Code Mode sandbox (a local JS isolate). Provider\n> Skills run entirely on the provider's infrastructure.\n\nSkills are **inert without an execution tool**. The execution tool activates the\nsandbox; skills are additional bundles that run inside it:\n\n- **Anthropic**: skills attach to `codeExecutionTool` (`@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools`).\n- **OpenAI**: skills nest inside `shellTool` (`@tanstack/ai-openai/tools`) and\n  require the Responses API.\n\nYou already have a `chat()` call working. By the end of this page you will have\nattached a hosted skill to the right execution tool, with the provider handling\nthe rest.\n\n---\n\n## Portable vs hosted skills\n\nThere are two ways to give a model skills in TanStack AI, and they solve\ndifferent problems:\n\n- **Portable skills** ([`withSkills`](../skills/agent-skills)) render a catalog\n  and let the model call `load_skill`. They run on any tool-calling model, need\n  no server sandbox, and read `SKILL.md` from a folder, a bundle, or your own\n  store. Reach for these first.\n- **Hosted (provider) skills**, this page, run inside the provider's server-side\n  sandbox and are referenced by ID. They are non-portable and require an\n  execution tool, but the provider does the running.\n\nUse hosted skills when you need the provider's sandbox (running code, producing\nfiles). Use portable skills for everything else.\n\nThe two do not mix in one `chat()` call. If you attach hosted skills to a\n`code_execution` or `shell` tool and also add `withSkills`, the middleware\nthrows: the model would see two catalogs and two protocols. Pick one delivery\nmode per call.\n\n---\n\n## Anthropic: skills via `codeExecutionTool`\n\n### 1. Install the package\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\nvue: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\npreact: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\nangular: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\noctane: @tanstack/ai-anthropic\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n### 2. Add the `codeExecutionTool` with skills\n\nImport `codeExecutionTool` from `@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools`, not from the\nadapter root. Pass a `skills` array as the second argument.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { codeExecutionTool } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic/tools'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-4-5'),\n    messages,\n    tools: [\n      codeExecutionTool(\n        { type: 'code_execution_20250825', name: 'code_execution' },\n        {\n          skills: [{ type: 'anthropic', skill_id: 'pptx', version: 'latest' }],\n        },\n      ),\n    ],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\nThe adapter automatically:\n\n- Lifts your skills into the request's top-level `container.skills` parameter\n  (the shape Anthropic's API requires).\n- Attaches the `code-execution-2025-08-25` beta header, plus the\n  `skills-2025-10-02` beta header when skills are present.\n\nYou do not set beta headers manually.\n\n### Skill shape\n\nEach entry in the `skills` array is an `AnthropicContainerSkill`:\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `type` | `'anthropic' \\| 'custom'` | yes | `'anthropic'` for Anthropic-hosted skills; `'custom'` for your own bundles. |\n| `skill_id` | `string` | yes | 1–64 characters. |\n| `version` | `string` | no | Specific version string, or `'latest'` (default when omitted). |\n\nUp to 8 skills per request. The factory throws at call time if you exceed this\nor supply an invalid `skill_id`.\n\n### Deprecation notice\n\nSetting skills via `modelOptions.container.skills` is deprecated. Use\n`codeExecutionTool(config, { skills })` instead — the legacy path bypasses the\nautomatic beta-header wiring.\n\n---\n\n## OpenAI: skills via `shellTool` (Responses API only)\n\nThe OpenAI `shellTool` accepts an `environment` object that can carry a\n`skills` array. This is **Responses API only**; the Chat Completions API does\nnot support the shell tool.\n\n### 1. Install the package\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-openai\nvue: @tanstack/ai-openai\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-openai\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-openai\npreact: @tanstack/ai-openai\nangular: @tanstack/ai-openai\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-openai\noctane: @tanstack/ai-openai\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n### 2. Add the `shellTool` with skills\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { shellTool } from '@tanstack/ai-openai/tools'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.2'),\n    messages,\n    tools: [\n      shellTool({\n        environment: {\n          type: 'container_auto',\n          skills: [\n            { type: 'skill_reference', skill_id: 'skill_abc', version: '2' },\n          ],\n        },\n      }),\n    ],\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\n### Skill shape\n\nEach entry in the `skills` array is a `SkillReference`:\n\n| Field | Type | Required | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `type` | `'skill_reference'` | yes | Always `'skill_reference'` for OpenAI. |\n| `skill_id` | `string` | yes | The skill identifier provided by OpenAI. |\n| `version` | `string` | no | A positive integer as a string (e.g. `'2'`) or `'latest'`. |\n\nNote: `version` is a string, not a number.\n\n---\n\n## Scope\n\nOnly **hosted, managed-by-id** skills are wired by these factories:\n\n- Anthropic: `type: 'anthropic'` or `type: 'custom'`\n- OpenAI: `type: 'skill_reference'`\n\nInline bundles, local-path references, and upload-API skill creation are not\nhandled by `codeExecutionTool` or `shellTool`.\n\n---\n\n## Related pages\n\n- [Portable Agent Skills](../skills/agent-skills) — the provider-agnostic\n  alternative: a catalog plus `load_skill`, on any tool-calling model.\n- [Provider Tools](./provider-tools.md) — all native provider tools and the\n  type-level guard that prevents pairing a tool with an unsupported model.\n- [Anthropic adapter → `codeExecutionTool`](../adapters/anthropic.md#codeexecutiontool)\n- [OpenAI adapter → `shellTool`](../adapters/openai.md#shelltool)\n"}
